# Next.js App Router Architectural Guidelines

## Core Principles

1. **Service-Based Data Layer**: Domain logic (queries, actions, clients) lives in `src/services/<service-name>/`.
2. **Thin `app/` Directory**: `src/app/` holds pages, layouts, and route handlers only — no business logic or UI.
3. **Shared UI / Hooks / Types**: Components, hooks, and types live at the `src/` root — not inside services.
4. **Server Components by Default**: Use RSC. Add `'use client'` only for state, effects, or event listeners.

## Folder Structure

```text
src/
├── app/                    # Routing only (pages, layouts, route handlers)
├── services/
│   └── <service-name>/
│       ├── actions/        # 'use server' mutations (Zod + DB writes)
│       ├── queries/        # Async reads (called by RSC / route handlers)
│       └── clients/        # Third-party SDK wrappers & API clients
├── components/             # UI components (RSC by default)
├── hooks/                  # React hooks ('use client' when required)
├── types/                  # TypeScript types & Zod schemas
└── lib/                    # Shared infra (db pool, env helpers)
```

## Do / Don't

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — logic and UI in the route file
// src/app/page.tsx
export default async function Page() {
  const rows = await db.query("SELECT * FROM items");
  return <ul>{rows.map(...)}</ul>;
}

// ✅ GOOD — thin route, service query, shared component
// src/app/page.tsx
import { ItemsList } from "@/components/items-list";
export default function Page() {
  return <ItemsList />;
}

// src/services/items/queries/get-items.ts
import type { Item } from "@/types/items";
export async function getItems(): Promise<Item[]> { /* DB read */ }

// src/components/items-list.tsx
import { getItems } from "@/services/items/queries/get-items";
export async function ItemsList() {
  const items = await getItems();
  return <ul>...</ul>;
}
```

## Conventions

- Route handlers in `src/app/api/**` only orchestrate; call `services/*/queries` or `actions`
- Import UI from `@/components/*`, types from `@/types/*`, hooks from `@/hooks/*`
- Name files by intent: `get-items.ts`, `create-item.ts`, `items-list.tsx`
